The purpose of Sections 2–4 is to keep vzctl free for end users and operators,
while blocking sale of the software and commercial "open-source polishing"
(OEM wrapping, proprietary bundling, paid forks, and paid hosted offerings of
vzctl itself).


0. Definitions

"Software" means this repository's source code, binaries, and documentation,
including any modified version or derivative work.

"You" means any individual or legal entity exercising rights under this License.

"Sell" means to charge, or arrange for others to charge, any fee, subscription,
license fee, royalty, or other consideration for:
  (a) the Software;
  (b) access to the Software;
  (c) a packaged distribution, mirror, binary build, installer, or container
      image of the Software; or
  (d) a fork, rebrand, "enterprise edition", "pro build", or substantially
      similar offering whose primary value is the Software.

"Commercial Product" means any software, appliance, platform, SDK, control
plane, GUI, or service that is sold, licensed for a fee, marketed as a paid
offering, or distributed under a proprietary / closed-source commercial
license.

"Bundle" means to embed, combine, wrap, rebrand, OEM, white-label, ship as a
component, or otherwise redistribute the Software as part of another product
or distribution, including thin wrappers whose primary functionality is the
Software.

"Provide as a Service" means to offer third parties remote access to the
Software's functionality (including via API, UI, CLI proxy, or managed
control plane), whether self-hosted on your infrastructure or multi-tenant.


