2. No Sale

You may not Sell the Software.

Prohibited (non-exhaustive):
  - selling vzctl, forks, or derivatives as a product;
  - paid redistribution of source or binaries;
  - paid "enterprise", "pro", "supported build", or branded forks whose
    primary deliverable is the Software;
  - charging for download, installers, container images, or access to the
    Software itself.

Allowed:
  - using the Software free of charge inside your own organization, including
    for commercial internal operations;
  - charging for genuine professional services that are not a pretext for
    Selling the Software (for example consulting, custom integration,
    training, or time-and-materials support), provided the Software itself
    remains available under this License at no charge and is not the product
    being sold.


3. No Commercial Bundling / No Open-Source Polishing

You may not Bundle the Software into a Commercial Product.

This section prohibits commercial redistributors and "open-source polishers"
that package, wrap, rebrand, or integrate the Software into a paid or
proprietary offering.

Prohibited (non-exhaustive):
  - embedding or shipping the Software inside a paid hypervisor, DevOps,
    virtualization, or lab-management product;
  - proprietary commercial GUIs, control planes, or appliances that
    redistribute or require the Software as a bundled component;
  - OEM / white-label distributions of the Software;
  - combining the Software with proprietary code into one Commercial Product
    that customers receive or run.

Allowed:
  - running the Software as a standalone tool in a commercial environment;
  - using the Software to build, host, or operate your own workloads and
    internal infrastructure;
  - combining the Software only with software that is itself licensed under
    this License or under AGPLv3 (or another strong copyleft that keeps the
    combination non-proprietary), provided the result is not Sold and is not
    offered as a Commercial Product.


4. No Commercial Hosted Offering of the Software

You may not Provide as a Service a Commercial Product whose primary purpose
or primary value is access to the Software or a thin wrapper around it.

Prohibited (non-exhaustive):
  - "managed vzctl", "vzctl cloud", or equivalent paid hosted offerings;
  - multi-tenant SaaS control planes that expose the Software's core
    functionality to paying customers;
  - paid remote access to forks/derivatives that are substantially the
    Software.

Allowed:
  - using the Software privately to operate your own unrelated services
    (the Software is infrastructure you run, not the product you sell to
    customers);
  - employees/contractors of your organization using the Software on your
    behalf, without providing the Software's functionality as a paid product
    to third parties.


5. No Circumvention

You may not do indirectly what this License prohibits directly, including
through affiliates, resellers, agents, "partner" SKUs, separate download
portals, dual packaging, or contracts that effectively Sell, Bundle, or
Provide as a Service the Software in violation of Sections 2–4.

Any attempt to relicense, sublicense, or redistribute the Software under
plain AGPL or any other terms that omit Sections 2–4 is void and is a
breach of this License.


